2. The Floats (float.frac)

This implements native IEEE-754 64-bit floats by treating them as exact rationals with powers-of-two denominators.

```frac
\ float.frac — IEEE-754 bidirectional bridge

\ Decode raw 64-bit float bits (addr) into an exact Rat
def f64->rat :addr
  addr @ :bits
  bits 63 >> 1 and :sign
  bits 52 >> 2047 and :exp
  bits 4503599627370495 and :mantissa
  
  exp if0 mantissa if0 0 exit then then
  exp 2047 - if0 sign if0 1/0 else -1/0 then exit then
  exp if0 else 4503599627370496 mantissa + :mantissa then
  
  exp 1023 - :shift
  shift 0 - if 1 shift neg 2 swap ^ / :val else 1 shift 2 swap ^ * :val then
  sign if0 val neg else val then
;

\ Encode exact Rat (p/q) into 64-bit float bits, rounding to 52 bits
def rat->f64 :q :p
  p if0 0 exit then
  p 0 - if 1 :sign p neg :p else 0 :sign then
  
  0 :exp
  begin p q - while p 2 / :p exp 1 + :exp repeat
  begin p 2 * q - - while p 2 * :p exp 1 - :exp repeat
  
  p q / p - :frac
  frac 4503599627370496 * 1/2 + floor :mantissa
  
  sign 63 <<  exp 1023 + 52 << or  mantissa or
;
```

