5. Multitasking (task.frac)

Right now, typing begin again freezes the machine. We can fix this using Cooperative Multitasking (which is much easier and safer for a toy OS) or Preemptive (using the APIC timer).

The C Micro-Runtime (Context Switching)
To multitask, you need to swap the rsp (stack pointer). When you swap the stack pointer, you are effectively swapping the brain of the CPU.

```c
// Add to kernel.c
static uint64_t* task_stacks[10];
static int current_task = 0;

HELPER void h_spawn(void* entry) {
    static int next_task = 1;
    task_stacks[next_task] = malloc(65536) + 65536; // 64KB stack, top-aligned
    // Push the entry point onto the new stack so `ret` jumps to it
    task_stacks[next_task][-1] = (uint64_t)entry; 
    next_task++;
}

HELPER void h_yield(void) {
    uint64_t rsp;
    __asm__ volatile("mov %%rsp, %0" : "=r"(rsp));
    task_stacks[current_task] = (uint64_t*)rsp;
    
    current_task = (current_task + 1) % 10; // simple round-robin
    while (task_stacks[current_task] == 0) current_task = (current_task + 1) % 10;
    
    __asm__ volatile("mov %0, %%rsp" : : "r"(task_stacks[current_task]));
    __asm__ volatile("ret"); // Pops the return address from the NEW stack
}
// Add to bootstrap(): add_word("spawn", h_spawn); add_word("yield", h_yield);
```

(Note: this is a simplified context switch. In reality, you also need to save/restore RBP, RBX, and R12-R15).

The Franc Scheduler (task.frac)
Now you can write the scheduler in Franc. You can spawn the calculator in the background, and a graphics demo in the foreground.

```frac
\ task.frac — Cooperative Multitasking
def task-counter
  0 :i
  begin
    i 1 + :i
    \ Draw the counter to the screen
    10 10 i ~ type
    \ Yield the CPU to the other tasks!
    yield
  again
;

def task-clock
  begin
    \ Read the CMOS real-time clock via I/O ports
    0x70 0x00 outb 0x71 inb :secs
    10 50 secs ~ type
    yield
  again
;

def main
  0 clearfb
  ' task-counter spawn
  ' task-clock spawn
  begin
    \ Main REPL loop (yields every time it waits for a key)
    key
    yield
  again
;
```

Now, the screen updates the clock and the counter while you are typing. If the REPL blocks, it yields to the clock.

The Final Upgrade: Preemptive Multitasking
If you want FracOS to be a real OS, you need to interrupt the begin again loop.

1. Enable the APIC Timer (Local APIC at 0xFEE00000).
2. Set it to fire an interrupt every 10 milliseconds.
3. In your C interrupt handler, call h_yield() before returning from the interrupt.

Because you have an IDT (Interrupt Descriptor Table), the CPU saves the current state automatically. The APIC timer just forces yield to happen. Now, you cannot freeze the OS with an infinite loop. It will just take up 1/Nth of the CPU time.

